    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tarquĭtĭus</span></b> ,
		ii, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an Etruscan proper name;</i> so esp. <i>the Etruscan Tarquitius</i>, <i>who
				wrote on divination</i>, <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 3, 7,
				2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 10, 2</span></i>; Plin.
			ind. libri 2.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tar-quĭtĭānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of Tarquitius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 25, 2, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
